  "reason": "Butler delegates longer work to Butler-mode subagents. Core: children of a Butler chat run with control_assistant (Butler's Core tools) on a provider model, including follow-up rounds; every lookup of Butler's own chat (reservation SQL, _settings_chat, active_control_assistant_session) skips them; a provider Butler delegates by default until butler_allow_subagents records the operator's choice, while unattended recovery reads settings without that default; delegation and child instructions are added to Butler's prompt. UI: Butler settings gain the delegation checkbox and Running at once (provider) or the provider-subagent picker (harness); the panel shows a subagent activity strip, renders posted reports as result cards and adds new reports live; the sidebar and Sessions page keep Butler, not a newer Butler-mode child, as the owner. Adds the butler-subagents settings destination, docs, product-help regression, workflow-registry inventory and a real-Core LAN Playwright journey. Python: new Butler subagent tests, Butler sessions/recovery (default must not reach recovery), runtime switching, control-plane reads, subagent choice/delivery/replay and harness provider subagents, the passing subagent and settings-assistant tests, product-help digest and search, and Playwright impact manifest tests. Frontend: Butler panel, new Butler subagent component tests, sidebar, settings list and assistant actions. Playwright: the new area on all eight real-Core assistant projects (desktop, compact, Chromium and WebKit at 320/390/430).",
